 series:"第三部 · 玻璃島",title:"When the River Rose",zh:"河水上漲時",scene:"night",blurb:"雨勢太大，這次他們得先救人，才有辦法繼續調查。",
 words:"dam extreme drown ambulance breathe breath swift scream",pages:[
 ["Extreme rain struck the island before sunset. The river below an old dam rose quickly, and the trail became slippery. A child slipped near the water. Noah heard a scream and saw the current carry the child away.","日落前，極端暴雨襲擊小島。老水壩下方的河水迅速上漲，小徑變得濕滑。一個孩子在水邊滑倒。Noah 聽見尖叫，看見急流把孩子沖走。"],
 ["A guide threw a rope, and a rescue worker pulled the child toward a shallow bank. Noah wanted to jump in, but the current was too swift; entering without equipment could have caused two people to drown. The child could breathe, though each breath was painful.","嚮導丟出繩子，救援人員把孩子拉往淺灘。Noah 想跳下去，但水流太急，沒裝備入水可能讓兩人都溺水。孩子還能呼吸，只是每次吸氣都會痛。"],
 ["An ambulance arrived, and a medic checked the injury. Nora stood quietly beside the child's family. The flood had washed away part of the riverside path. Their trip would have to pause, but everyone agreed that keeping people safe mattered more than the report.","救護車趕到，醫護人員檢查傷勢。Nora 靜靜站在孩子家人旁。洪水沖走了河岸步道的一部分。調查必須暫停，但大家都同意人命安全比報告重要。"]],
 quiz:[["What made the trail dangerous?","Extreme rain and rising water","A crowded festival","A lack of maps","A broken elevator","暴雨使水上漲、步道濕滑。"],["Why did Noah not jump into the river?","It could endanger another person","He could not swim in a pool","He had lost his shoes","The river was empty","沒有設備入水可能造成第二名溺水者。"],["What happened after the rescue?","A medic checked the child's injury","The resort opened","The ferry departed","The map was destroyed","救護車到場，醫護檢查孩子傷勢。"]]
