 series:"第三部 · 玻璃島",title:"The Public Meeting",zh:"公開會議",scene:"meeting",blurb:"每個人都想發言，但證據和意見必須被分開。",
 words:"represent comparison acceptable outline summary restrict desirable",pages:[
 ["At the public meeting, Nora was asked to represent the research team. She brought a comparison of the old map and the new one. Her outline showed which areas had changed, but she explained that the maps alone could not identify who had ordered the change.","公開會議上，Nora 受邀代表研究團隊。她帶來新舊地圖的比較。大綱指出變動的區域，但她也解釋，單靠地圖無法指出是誰下令更改。"],
 ["The developer offered what he called a reasonable plan: keep the resort but restrict access to the damaged bay. A fisherman answered that this was not acceptable because his family worked there. Another resident asked whether a smaller building would be more desirable.","開發商提出他所謂合理的方案：保留度假村，但限制進入受損海灣。漁夫說這無法接受，因為家人就在那裡工作。另一位居民問，縮小建築規模是否會更理想。"],
 ["Noah wrote a summary of the different suggestions without choosing for the community. The meeting ended with a promise to release the full test results. Outside, Nora said, 'A real decision begins when everyone can see the same information.'", "Noah 把不同建議整理成摘要，沒有替社區做決定。會議最後承諾公布完整檢驗結果。走到外面，Nora 說：「真正的決定，始於每個人都能看到相同的資訊。」"]],
